      "writtenOn": "2026-09-22T06:04:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re right — nobody should ever need to set permissions on that pattern. It\u0027s a defensive branch, not a live path: a direct push to a refs/changes/* ref is rejected by the create/push permission checks before commit validation runs (verified with an acceptance test — it fails at the create gate, then the create-new-objects gate), so the merge scoping never resolves to refs/for/refs/changes/\u003cn\u003e in practice. I reworded the javadoc to describe the exclusion as defensive rather than implying refs/for/refs/changes/... is a normal outcome.",
      "parentUuid": "50cff5a3_21228b39",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 242,
        "startChar": 66,
        "endLine": 242,
        "endChar": 91
